    cura_en: "It has no chronograph pushers in the mechanical sense: start/stop/reset are electronically driven, and the pushers act on a circuit, not a cam or a lever. They remain water-entry points like any case pusher, though, so the usual rule applies: don't press them underwater or with the watch wet. After a battery change, the chronograph hands may not return exactly to zero: an electrical reset procedure is needed, which on this calibre runs through the circuit rather than a manual mechanical alignment. No service interval is stated by the maker, consistent with a module meant to be replaced, not repaired.",
